[center][size=5][color=#E0B062][b]Magic Quest Log[/b][/color][/size]
[size=3][i]The quest and deed atlas for Middle-earth - right inside LOTRO[/i][/size]

[b]15,118 quests | 5,528 deeds | English, German and French[/b]

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]A better way to find your next adventure[/b][/color][/size]
Magic Quest Log puts the enormous LOTRO quest and deed catalog into one fast, searchable in-game window. Find the story you want to continue, see what is available in a landscape, check your progress, and open the exact recorded location in MoorMap.

Your companion website is [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de][b]LOTRO Log Book[/b][/url]. It expands the in-game atlas with interactive maps, quest-giver pages, items, recipes, factions, landmarks, instances, adventures and a travel planner.

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Inside the plugin[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]One clear quest tree.[/b] Landscapes and thematic groups are shown together: Eriador, Rhovanion, Rohan, Gondor, Mordor, Haradwaith and Rhun, followed by Epic Story, Class Quests, Origin Quests, Festivals and Events, Missions, Instances and Battles, Crafting and Other Quests.
[*][b]Epic story at a glance.[/b] Epic quests are organized by volume and book instead of being mixed into ordinary area lists.
[*][b]Search everything.[/b] Search by part of a quest, deed or area name. Search ignores case and accents.
[*][b]Explore without spoilers.[/b] Read the description, quest giver and requirements first. Steps and objectives remain hidden until you ask for them.
[*][b]Use practical filters.[/b] Show All, Open, Done or Available entries. Available checks known requirements and your character level, but cannot verify every condition in the game.
[*][b]Track your journey.[/b] Imported progress and completions seen in the quest channel are shown with clear checks and completed/total counts.
[*][b]Switch characters.[/b] Keep several imported characters in the same installation and switch between them from the Character button.
[*][b]Open locations in MoorMap.[/b] Use the recorded quest-giver position, or reveal objectives and open a recorded objective position.
[*][b]Use your language.[/b] The plugin follows the LOTRO client language: English, German or French.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]LOTRO Log Book - more than a quest list[/b][/color][/size]
[url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de][b]LOTRO Log Book[/b][/url] is the free companion site for planning and completing your journey through Middle-earth.

[list]
[*]Interactive maps for quests, deeds, landscapes and adventures
[*]Quest-giver and landmark browsers
[*]Searchable items, recipes, factions and instances
[*]A travel planner for routes, stable masters and travel skills
[*]Personal progress stored locally in your browser
[*]Companion progress import without uploading your character files
[/list]

The site works without an account and does not require a subscription. Start with the [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de/de/karte/][b]quest map[/b][/url] or open the [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de/spielstand.html?lang=en][b]progress page[/b][/url].

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Installing or updating[/b][/color][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Close LOTRO before replacing plugin files.
[*]Open your LOTRO [b]Plugins[/b] folder. On a Mac this is usually [font=Courier New]~/Documents/The Lord of the Rings Online/Plugins[/font]. On Windows it is normally inside your Documents folder.
[*]Extract [b]MagicQuestLog-0.5.4.zip[/b] into Plugins. The final path must be [font=Courier New]Plugins\MagicQuestLog\MagicQuestLog.plugin[/font], not [font=Courier New]Plugins\MagicQuestLog\MagicQuestLog\MagicQuestLog.plugin[/font].
[*]Start LOTRO and load the plugin with [font=Courier New]/plugins load MagicQuestLog[/font]. In German: [font=Courier New]/zusatzmodule laden MagicQuestLog[/font].
[*]Open it with [font=Courier New]/mql[/font].
[/list]

Keep your [b]PluginData[/b] folder when updating. It contains your settings and progress files. If you need to bring older progress into the plugin, use the [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de/spielstand.html?lang=en][b]progress page on LOTRO Log Book[/b][/url]; the website provides the current instructions and writes the result into PluginData.

Only the map button needs [url=https://www.lotrointerface.com/downloads/info532-MoorMap.html]MoorMap[/url] by Garan. The rest of the plugin works without it.

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]What is new in 0.5.4[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]One combined task view.[/b] Landscapes and thematic groups now appear as equal top-level nodes. There is no confusing mode switch between landscape and topic.
[*][b]Clearer categories.[/b] Epic Story, Class Quests, Origin Quests, Festivals and Events, Missions, Instances and Battles, Crafting and Other Quests are easy to reach beside the landscape groups.
[*][b]The existing progress model stays safe.[/b] Quest ids, deed ids, imported progress and live completion tracking are unchanged.
[*]The catalog still contains 15,118 quests and 5,528 deeds in all three languages.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Earlier improvements[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]0.5.3:[/b] Exact duplicate class deeds are shown once while progress under older ids remains recognized.
[*][b]0.5.2:[/b] Monster-play deeds no longer inflate normal-character totals.
[*][b]0.5.1:[/b] Companion imports, accented character names and character switching are more reliable.
[*][b]0.5.0:[/b] Landscape-first navigation, epic volumes and books, split catalog loading and objectives on request.
[/list]

